# `using` requires the disposal protocol; this resource never releases anything.

error async/invalid-disposable fixtures/async/invalid-disposable.ts:7 in withResource
  message: withResource binds resource with using, which requires the Symbol.dispose protocol that resource does not provide
  7 |   using resource = open();
    |   ^
  binding: resource = open()
  because: the type of resource declares no [Symbol.dispose] method, so leaving the scope releases nothing
  hint: give the resource a Symbol.dispose or Symbol.asyncDispose method, or bind it with const instead of using

error async/disposed-resource-escape fixtures/async/invalid-disposable.ts:8 in withResource
  message: withResource lets resource escape through return but disposes it before the caller can use it
  8 |   return resource;
    |   ^
  binding: resource = open()
  because: the using scope disposes resource before this function returns, so the caller receives a released resource
  hint: stop the resource from escaping its disposal scope, or hand the caller an owned resource instead

